Everything is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:

### Changes to `src/commands_memory.rs`:

1. Updated imports — Added add_memory_with_category, is_valid_category, and `MEMORY_CATEGORIES from memory.rs; removed unused add_memory` from the main imports (it's still imported in the test module).

2. **Added `parse_category_prefix** — A helper function that parses [category:X] prefix syntax from a note string. Returns (category, remaining_note). Falls back to ("general", full_note)` when:
   • No [category: prefix is present
   • The category is not in MEMORY_CATEGORIES (invalid)
   • The note after the prefix is empty or whitespace-only

3. Updated `handle_remember` — Now calls parse_category_prefix to extract category, uses add_memory_with_category instead of add_memory, shows category in the confirmation message (for non-general categories), and updated usage text to show category syntax with examples.

4. Updated `handle_memories` — Both the "show all" and "search results" paths now display a [category] tag next to each memory entry (e.g., `[0] [build] always run cargo fmt (2 hours ago)`).

5. Added 5 new tests:
   • `test_parse_category_prefix_with_valid_category — verifies [category:build]` parsing
   • test_parse_category_prefix_without_category — defaults to "general"
   • `test_parse_category_prefix_invalid_category` — unknown categories fall back to "general"
   • test_parse_category_prefix_all_valid_categories — all 5 categories parse correctly
   • test_parse_category_prefix_empty_note_after_prefix — edge case: prefix with no note
   • test_parse_category_prefix_whitespace_only_after_prefix — edge case: prefix with only whitespace
